dsh-alioth is an independent, native consumer of the Alioth model — a
sibling of AppCreator under the same model, NOT a consumer of AppCreator's
products (its generated applications, its service code, or its runtime).

The Alioth model's open distribution is published by the AppCreator
open-source project:

    https://github.com/CosmicTools9/AppCreator
    Copyright 2026 The Alioth Authors
    Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0

From that distribution, model snapshots pulled by @dsh-alioth/env-alioth
(cache under <dataRoot>/models) carry the model artifacts this plugin
consumes: the isahl_meta registry bootstrap baseline
(`backend/ddl/*isahl_meta*.sql`), the skill-adapter definitions
(`skill-adapters/*.yaml`), and the vendored model sources used as the
version anchor. AppCreator's own application artifacts (`app_creator`
persistence DDL, service code, generated apps) are excluded from
consumption by design.

Following that open-source license, this repository is licensed under
Apache-2.0 (see LICENSE). License notes on the distribution: the
authoritative upstream checkout carries an Apache-2.0 LICENSE file, while
the public GitHub tree currently ships WITHOUT any LICENSE file and its
Cargo.toml metadata says MIT. The LICENSE file from the authoritative tree
prevails; the LICENSE in this repository serves as the compliant copy for
the model artifacts handled here. Upstream should publish LICENSE on the
public tree and align its Cargo metadata.

Native implementations of Alioth model pipeline semantics in this
repository carry this attribution and remain under Apache-2.0. Upstream
carries no NOTICE file at the time of writing.
